The '''[[2022–23 in Scottish football|2022–23 season]]''' was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s 129th season of competitive football.

==Pre-season and friendlies==
Celtic held a pre-season training camp in [[Bad Erlach]] (Austria),<ref name="Austria_friendlies">{{cite web | url=https://www.celticfc.com/news/2022/may/05/celtic-return-to-austria-for-2022-23-pre-season-training-camp/ | title=Celtic return to Austria for 2022/23 pre-season training camp | publisher=Celtic FC | date=5 May 2022 | access-date=12 May 2022}}</ref> where they played friendlies against Wiener Viktoria and [[SK Rapid Wien|Rapid Wien]]. The camp ended with a trip across the border to face [[FC Baník Ostrava|Baník Ostrava]] in a match celebrating the Czechs' centenary year.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.celticfc.com/news/2022/may/06/celts-to-take-part-in-banik-ostrava-pre-season-centenary-game/ | title=Celtic to play in special anniversary match in Czech Republic | publisher=Celtic FC | date=6 May 2022 | access-date=12 May 2022}}</ref> On Celtic's return to Glasgow, they played [[Blackburn Rovers F.C.|Blackburn Rovers]].<ref name="Austria_friendlies"/> A trip to Poland followed, where they faced [[Legia Warsaw]] in a match honouring the career of former Celtic goalkeeper [[Artur Boruc]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.celticfc.com/news/2022/june/10/celtic-to-honour-the-great-artur-boruc-in-poland/ | title=Celtic to honour the great Artur Boruc in Poland | publisher=Celtic FC | date=10 June 2022 | access-date=10 June 2022}}</ref> Celtic's pre-season schedule concluded with [[Norwich City F.C.|Norwich City]]'s visit to Celtic Park.<ref name="Austria_friendlies"/>

